# Local build → try → commit

When finishing feature/bug work in this repo (not docs-only):

1. Run `.\build.ps1` only (clears stale `RUSTFLAGS`, uses `D:\mingw64`, tests + release → `release\ssms-search-rs.exe`). Do not invent alternate linkers.
2. Confirm the script exits 0 and `release\README.txt` has a fresh Built timestamp.
3. Leave the exe for the user to try (`release\ssms-search-rs.exe` is gitignored).
4. Then commit code + `release\README.txt` (+ this rule if changed).

Do not claim done without a successful `.\build.ps1` in the session. Do not commit `.superpowers/` or `docs/superpowers/briefs/` scratch.
